IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`

-- g4-art12-name.l4: Article 12 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the name of a charity. Which names are undesirable, the registered name and number, changing a name or adding an alternative,
-- and the prohibition on using any other name. Imports only prelude, domain and modules of group G4; the Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1) is an input, never computed.
-- Time. Part 4 (Articles 8 to 17) came into force on 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018); whether it is in force on a day is the integrator's wrapper, not a gate here (PLAN section 10). No entry in the Table of Endnote References
-- amends Articles 11 or 12, so one text of them is encoded for every vintage; only the identity of "the Minister" (Article 1) varies by vintage, and the rules here are typed by the ROLE `the Minister`.
-- Forks read here: F4.5 (is a formerly registered charity "another registered charity"), F4.7 (which names of another charity are compared), F4.8 (is a previous registered name still "its registered name").

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `Article 12 -- Name of charity`

§§§ `Article 12(1) -- the name is undesirable`

-- F4.5: who is "any other registered charity". Article 1: a registered charity is "an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register".
-- src:34 | “registered charity” means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register;
@ref Article 1 "registered charity" (src:34)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the holder of the name stands on the register
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` IF
    CONSIDER standing
    WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:34 | “registered charity” means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register;
@ref Article 1 "registered charity" (src:34)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the holder of the name stands on the register
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` IF
    CONSIDER standing
    WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- F4.7: which of the names entered for that charity are "the name of" it.
-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
@ref Article 12(1)(a) (src:355)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register` @desc How the name is entered for its holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.7 reading A: the registered name and the alternative registered names` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the registered name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an alternative registered name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a previous registered name` THEN FALSE

-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
@ref Article 12(1)(a) (src:355)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register` @desc How the name is entered for its holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.7 reading B: the registered name only` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the registered name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an alternative registered name` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a previous registered name` THEN FALSE

-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
@ref Article 12(1)(a) (src:355)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register` @desc How the name is entered for its holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.7 reading C: every name entered, previous names included` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the registered name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an alternative registered name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a previous registered name` THEN TRUE

-- Ground (a): the entry that the Commissioner is of the opinion is the same as, or too similar to, the proposed name is the name of "any other registered charity" only if it is held by another entity,
-- that entity stands as a registered charity (F4.5) and the entry is one of the names compared (F4.7).
-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
@ref Article 12(1)(a) (src:355)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  entry IS A `Name entered in the register` @desc An entry of the register that the Commissioner is of the opinion is the same as, or too similar to, the name in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1)(a) the entry is the name of another registered charity` IF
        NOT entry's `held by the entity itself`
    AND (CONSIDER interp's `whether a formerly registered charity is another registered charity`
         WHEN `a formerly registered charity is not another registered charity` THEN `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` (entry's `standing of the entity that holds it`)
         WHEN `a formerly registered charity is another registered charity` THEN `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` (entry's `standing of the entity that holds it`))
    AND (CONSIDER interp's `which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares`
         WHEN `its registered name and its alternative registered names` THEN `F4.7 reading A: the registered name and the alternative registered names` (entry's `kind of entry`)
         WHEN `its registered name only` THEN `F4.7 reading B: the registered name only` (entry's `kind of entry`)
         WHEN `every name entered for it in the register, previous names included` THEN `F4.7 reading C: every name entered, previous names included` (entry's `kind of entry`))

-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
@ref Article 12(1)(a) (src:355)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1), for the name in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` IF
    any (GIVEN entry YIELD `Art 12(1)(a) the entry is the name of another registered charity` interp entry) (opinion's `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name`)

-- src:356 | (b) is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity;
@ref Article 12(1)(b) (src:356)
GIVEN opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1), for the name in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1)(b) the name is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IF
    opinion's `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity`

-- src:357 | (c) gives the impression that the entity is connected to any person to which it is not connected, whether in Jersey or elsewhere; or
@ref Article 12(1)(c) (src:357)
GIVEN opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1), for the name in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1)(c) the name gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IF
    opinion's `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected`

-- src:358 | (d) is offensive.
@ref Article 12(1)(d) (src:358)
GIVEN opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1), for the name in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1)(d) the name is offensive` IF
    opinion's `offensive`

-- src:354 | (1) For the purpose of Article 11(4)(e), the name of an entity is undesirable as the registered name of a charity if, in the opinion of the Commissioner, the name –
-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
-- src:356 | (b) is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity;
-- src:357 | (c) gives the impression that the entity is connected to any person to which it is not connected, whether in Jersey or elsewhere; or
-- src:358 | (d) is offensive.
@ref Article 12(1) (src:354-358)
@export Whether a name is undesirable as the registered name of a charity, because in the Commissioner's opinion it is the same as or too similar to the name of another registered charity, likely to mislead the public, gives the impression of a connection with a person it is not connected to, or is offensive (Article 12(1); standard fact IP18); on the readings given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on each ground of Article 12(1) for the name in question; ground (a) is given as the entries of the register that the Commissioner is of the opinion are the same as or too similar to the name
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` IF
        `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` interp opinion
    OR  `Art 12(1)(b) the name is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` opinion
    OR  `Art 12(1)(c) the name gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` opinion
    OR  `Art 12(1)(d) the name is offensive` opinion

§§§ `Article 12(2) -- the registered name and the registration number`

-- src:359 | (2) If the Commissioner registers the entity, the Commissioner must –
-- src:360 | (a) enter the name of the entity in the register (the “registered name”); and
@ref Article 12(2)(a) (src:359-360)
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the Commissioner has registered the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has registered the entity`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` (`the entity`'s name))
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b): the Commissioner allocates a number and enters it. The number is whatever the Commissioner allocates; the Law fixes no form for it and says nothing of its uniqueness (Article 17(1)(b) forbids only
-- assigning a deregistered entity's number to another registered charity).
-- src:359 | (2) If the Commissioner registers the entity, the Commissioner must –
-- src:361 | (b) allocate a number in respect of the registration, and enter that number (“the registration number”) in the register.
@ref Article 12(2)(b) (src:359) (src:361)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has registered the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(2)(b) the Commissioner must allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has registered the entity`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` allocated)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:359 | (2) If the Commissioner registers the entity, the Commissioner must –
@ref Article 12(2) (src:359)
@export The duties of the Commissioner, if the Commissioner registers the entity, to enter its name in the register as the registered name and to allocate a registration number and enter it (Article 12(2)); FULFILLED where the entity has not been registered
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the Commissioner has registered the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has registered the entity as a charity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(2) the Commissioner must enter the registered name and allocate and enter a number` IS
        `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` `the entity` `the Commissioner has registered the entity`
    RAND `Art 12(2)(b) the Commissioner must allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` `the Commissioner has registered the entity`

§§§ `Article 12(3) to (6) -- a change of name or an alternative name`

-- src:362 | (3) A registered charity may apply to the Commissioner for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name.
@ref Article 12(3) (src:362)
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity: entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(3) a registered charity may apply for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name` IS
    IF `the entity is a registered charity`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MAY `Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`apply for permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name` `the kind of change sought`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4): "The Commissioner must refuse permission if, in his or her opinion, any of the grounds in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of paragraph (1) applies in relation to the proposed name." Those four grounds are
-- exactly the grounds on which Article 12(1) makes a name undesirable, so the standard fact IP18, evaluated for the proposed name, is the condition. The Law states no duty to grant when no ground applies and no time.
-- src:363 | (4) The Commissioner must refuse permission if, in his or her opinion, any of the grounds in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of paragraph (1) applies in relation to the proposed name.
@ref Article 12(4) (src:363)
@export The duty of the Commissioner to refuse permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name when, in the Commissioner's opinion, a ground of Article 12(1) applies to the proposed name (Article 12(4)); FULFILLED where none does
GIVEN
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(4) the Commissioner must refuse permission to change or add a name` IS
    IF `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, `refuse permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:363 | (4) The Commissioner must refuse permission if, in his or her opinion, any of the grounds in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of paragraph (1) applies in relation to the proposed name.
@ref Article 12(4) (src:363)
@export The decision of the Commissioner on an application for permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name, as other provisions name it: that the Commissioner refuses (Article 12(4)); NOTHING where Article 12(4) obliges no refusal, because the Law then leaves the decision to the Commissioner
GIVEN
  `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the name of the applicant is, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable as the registered name of a charity on a ground in Article 12(1)(a) to (d)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner`
DECIDE `Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` IS
    IF `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`
    THEN JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5): the Commissioner enters the name "if the Commissioner grants permission, and the registered charity notifies the Commissioner that it has changed or added the name accordingly". "Accordingly" is read
-- as: the name notified is the name for which permission was granted, and the charity has done what the permission was for (changed the registered name, or added an alternative).
-- src:364 | (5) If the Commissioner grants permission, and the registered charity notifies the Commissioner that it has changed or added the name accordingly, the Commissioner must enter on the register the new or alternative registered name.
@ref Article 12(5) (src:364)
@export The duty of the Commissioner to enter on the register the new or alternative registered name when permission was granted and the charity notified that it has changed or added the name accordingly (Article 12(5)); FULFILLED where either condition fails
GIVEN `permission was granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner granted permission
      `the name for which permission was granted` IS A STRING @desc The name for which permission was granted
      `the change for which permission was granted` IS A `Kind of change of a registered name` @desc Whether the permission was to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name
      `the charity notified the Commissioner that it has changed or added the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity notified the Commissioner that it has changed or added the name
      `the name notified` IS A STRING @desc The name the charity notified
      `the change notified` IS A `Kind of change of a registered name` @desc Whether the charity notified a change of the registered name or the addition of an alternative registered name
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` IS
    IF     `permission was granted`
       AND `the charity notified the Commissioner that it has changed or added the name`
       AND `the name notified` EQUALS `the name for which permission was granted`
       AND `the change notified` EQUALS `the change for which permission was granted`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the new or alternative registered name in the register` `the name notified` `the change notified`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:365 | (6) If a registered charity reports a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b), the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name under paragraph (3).
@ref Article 12(6) (src:365)
@export The power of the Commissioner to require a registered charity to apply to change its registered name, when the charity has reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b) (Article 12(6)); FULFILLED where it has not
GIVEN `the charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(6) the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name` IS
    IF `the charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, `require the charity to apply to change its registered name`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The decision of Article 12(6) as other provisions name it (Article 33(2)(c) lets the charity appeal "to require the charity, under Article 12(6), to apply to change its registered name"):
-- the Commissioner requires (does what was proposed) or does not. Whether the Commissioner requires is a discretion, so it is an input.
-- src:365 | (6) If a registered charity reports a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b), the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name under paragraph (3).
@ref Article 12(6) (src:365)
GIVEN `the charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)
      `the Commissioner requires the charity to apply to change its registered name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exercised the power and required the charity to apply
GIVETH A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner`
DECIDE `Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` IS
    IF NOT `the charity reported a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Commissioner requires the charity to apply to change its registered name`
         THEN JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)
         ELSE JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`, `the Commissioner refuses`)

§§§ `Article 12(7) -- the names a registered charity may use`

-- F4.8: "its registered name or one of its registered names". Reading A: the names registered now, the registered name and the alternative registered names. Reading B adds the previous registered
-- names that Article 8(3)(l) keeps on the register.
-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
@ref Article 12(7)(a) (src:367)
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name and its alternative registered names
      used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.8 reading A: only the names registered now` IF
        used's `name used` EQUALS `the registered charity`'s `registered name`
    OR  elem (used's `name used`) (`the registered charity`'s `alternative registered names`)

-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
@ref Article 12(7)(a) (src:367)
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name and its alternative registered names
      used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.8 reading B: the previous registered names as well` IF
        used's `name used` EQUALS `the registered charity`'s `registered name`
    OR  elem (used's `name used`) (`the registered charity`'s `alternative registered names`)
    OR  elem (used's `name used`) (used's `previous registered names of the charity`)

-- src:366 | (7) A registered charity must not use any name other than –
-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
@ref Article 12(7)(a) (src:366-367)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name and its alternative registered names
  used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(7)(a) the name used is its registered name or one of its registered names` IF
    CONSIDER interp's `whether a previous registered name is still one of its registered names`
    WHEN `a previous registered name is not one of its registered names` THEN `F4.8 reading A: only the names registered now` `the registered charity` used
    WHEN `a previous registered name is still one of its registered names` THEN `F4.8 reading B: the previous registered names as well` `the registered charity` used

-- (b): "another name that (i) is related to such a name, and (ii) is not, in the opinion of the Commissioner, undesirable within the meaning of paragraph (1), in the context in which it is used."
-- "Related" is not defined by the Law: whether the name is related to a registered name is a fact the caller supplies. The Commissioner's opinion is on the four grounds of Article 12(1) as they bear on the name
-- in the context in which it is used.
-- src:368 | (b) another name that –
-- src:369 | (i) is related to such a name, and
-- src:370 | (ii) is not, in the opinion of the Commissioner, undesirable within the meaning of paragraph (1), in the context in which it is used.
@ref Article 12(7)(b) (src:368-370)
GIVEN used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(7)(b) the name used is related to a registered name and is not undesirable in its context` IF
        used's `related to one of the charity's registered names`
    AND NOT used's `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner`

-- "A registered charity": Article 1 defines it as an entity entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register. An entity in the historic section is not bound by the prohibition.
-- src:34 | “registered charity” means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register;
-- src:366 | (7) A registered charity must not use any name other than –
@ref Article 12(7) and Article 1 "registered charity" (src:34) (src:366)
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity; its entity stands in the general section, the restricted section or the historic section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(7) the entity is a registered charity` IF
    CONSIDER `the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register`
    WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:366 | (7) A registered charity must not use any name other than –
-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
-- src:368 | (b) another name that –
-- src:369 | (i) is related to such a name, and
-- src:370 | (ii) is not, in the opinion of the Commissioner, undesirable within the meaning of paragraph (1), in the context in which it is used.
@ref Article 12(7) (src:366-370)
@export Whether the name a registered charity uses is one it may use: its registered name or one of its registered names, or another name that is related to one and is not, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable in the context in which it is used (Article 12(7)); on the readings given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name and its alternative registered names
  used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` IF
        `Art 12(7)(a) the name used is its registered name or one of its registered names` interp `the registered charity` used
    OR  `Art 12(7)(b) the name used is related to a registered name and is not undesirable in its context` used

-- src:366 | (7) A registered charity must not use any name other than –
-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
-- src:368 | (b) another name that –
-- src:369 | (i) is related to such a name, and
-- src:370 | (ii) is not, in the opinion of the Commissioner, undesirable within the meaning of paragraph (1), in the context in which it is used.
@ref Article 12(7) (src:366-370)
@export The prohibition on a registered charity using a name it may not use (Article 12(7)): for the name used, FULFILLED if the name is permitted, otherwise a standing prohibition that using the name breaches; the Law states no penalty for it (its only consequence is through misconduct)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity: its registered name and its alternative registered names
  used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name the charity uses, with the facts Article 12(7) turns on
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 12`
DECIDE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` IS
    IF     NOT `Art 12(7) the entity is a registered charity` `the registered charity`
        OR `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` interp `the registered charity` used
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `a registered charity`
         SHANT `Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` (used's `name used`))
